        \sup_{\gamma\in\Gamma'}\normtemp{\mathscr{R}_{\gamma} - \mathscr{R}_{\mathds{1}}}_{\mathscr{L}({H}_\diamond^s(\partial\Omega);H^t(\partial\Omega)/\mathbb{C})}\leq \widetilde{C}_{s,t}\frac{M}{m}<\infty
    \end{align}
    as asserted.

    To finish the proof, we must show the first assertion of the lemma. The usual boundary trace and stability theorems applied to the harmonic function  $u_{\mathds{1},g}$ give
    \begin{align*}
