	Let $\gamma\in\Gamma'$, $\gamma_0\in\Gamma'$, and $s$ and $t$ be arbitrary. Denote the shifted NtD maps by $\widetilde{\mathscr{R}}_{\gamma}\coloneqq \mathscr{R}_{\gamma}-\mathscr{R}_{\mathds{1}}$ and $\widetilde{\mathscr{R}}_{\gamma_0}\coloneqq \mathscr{R}_{\gamma_0} - \mathscr{R}_{\mathds{1}}$. Let $\normtemp{{\,\cdot\,}}$ denote the $\mathrm{HS}(H^s_\diamond({\partial\Omega});H^t({\partial\Omega})/\mathbb{C})$ norm for brevity. We begin with the triangle inequality. For any $J\in\mathbb{N}$, it holds that
